<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isle of Mull</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Isle of Mull is the second-largest island of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-hebrides">Inner Hebrides</a>, off the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a>, separated from the mainland by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oresund">the Sound</a> of Mull. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it lay within the Gaelic kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, close to the monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iona">Iona</a> off its western tip, and it later belonged to the Lordship of the Isles and the Macleans of Duart. Its chief town is Tobermory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isle-of-mull.jpg" alt="Isle of Mull" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Clydiee · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tobermory_waterfront_recrop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
